The sysrq panic-seed's pstore `dmesg-ramoops-0` (proves the panic -> kmsg_dump ->
pstore capture path, triggered by `echo c > /proc/sysrq-trigger` on the
batch-8 detector kernel; does not exercise the soft-lockup detector itself).
Its head (boot banner, kernel command line) and the crash lines (the sysrq
trigger through the panic call trace). 326 lines, 23978 bytes total; md5
e5ad0ce5a7a0fb19138a9d1ce4330bbe. The MAC on the command line is redacted; the
full 326-line copy is not committed. Mounted read-only (`mount -t pstore -o ro
pstore /sys/fs/pstore`), copied, unmounted; nothing in pstore was deleted.

